    {
      "id": "c.unwind",
      "kind": "mechanism",
      "text": "Each factorial return hands its value to the call that made it, one frame down. factorial(2) gets 1 and returns 2 × 1 = 2.",
      "justification": "6.8.6.4p3: a return with an expression gives its value to the caller as the value of the call expression. factorial(1) was called by factorial(2) in line 7, so factorial(2) computes r = 2 * 1 = 2 and returns it. The run printed factorial(2) = 2 as line 5.",
      "sources": [
        {
          "title": "ISO/IEC 9899:2018 (C17), working draft N2176",
          "url": "https://www.open-std.org/jtc1/sc22/wg14/www/docs/n2176.pdf",
          "clause": "§6.8.6.4 ¶3",
          "quote": "If a return statement with an expression is executed, the value of the expression is returned to the caller as the value of the function call expression."
        },
